  // CLIMBERS · movement · flank (App. A.4, B.4). A pack of packSize paces paceOut m out for paceSeconds, then mounts any gap
  // held by fewer players (within countRadius) than it has Climbers, scrabbling scrabbleSeconds first. Up, they traverse
  // at traverseSpeed and go into the first unlit or empty car; a lone player in there is taken over takeSeconds. Into an
  // unlit car with every door and its hatch shut, they force their way in through the roof (the hatch torn off, on a cargo
  // car): the car's breached (spec B.9, train.json breach). breachLitCars: a lit car they get into because nobody's in it
  // too (the decision named only the unlit car; ARCHITECTURE §8). Note 272 (App. F.1, no chip damage): inside, a hit every
  // 3 s (were 25 every 1.5 s).
  "climbers": {
    // GDD §23 "lights fail" (note 183): coming over the engine's end into the cab, it smashes the forward lamp for this
    // long (s). Lamp armour (campaign.json, F.3) shortens it.
    "lampOutSeconds": 45,
    "paceOut": 2.5, "paceSeconds": 6, "catch": 1.2, "maxSpeed": 18, "loseBehind": 60, "scrabbleSeconds": 2.5, "holdReach": 2,
    "maxTries": 3, "traverseSpeed": 2.2, "reach": 1.8, "biteDamage": 35, "biteEvery": 3, "boredSeconds": 120, "health": 3,
    "minGaps": 2, "minSpeed": 5, "perGapWeight": 0.5, "packSize": [2, 3], "countRadius": 8, "takeSeconds": 10,
    "breachLitCars": false,
    // Note 288 (drivenOff; "outnumber them at the gaps"): up on the roofs or in a car, outnumbered where it is (more crew than
    // Climbers within countRadius) with no gang striking it, it drops back off after outnumberedSeconds (letting go) for
    // another gap. A lone blow knocks it off a friend; only the gang's blows take its health.
    "drivenOff": true, "outnumberedSeconds": 2,
    // Boarding-first (the director's decisions of 6 Oct 2026, GDD App. F.1; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 286): "slowing opens the
    // doors ... tight curves are where things board". They get a grip at the gap only with the train under mountBelow (m/s,
    // 50 km/h). Faster, they run on alongside, pacing it (the telegraph: a pack beside the train, waiting for it to slow),
    // and give it up waitForSlowSeconds after their pace; and the director sends them at speed at atSpeedWeight of their
    // weight. Slow on a tight bend (radius tightBendRadius m or less under the train or within bendAheadM ahead: a frontier
    // line's tightest, 300 m, is boarded at 14 m/s) they come bendWeight times as often. The counter: keep her over 50, or
    // hold the gaps as she takes the bend. Their door rule stands as decided 1 Oct: shut doors don't stop them; a dark car
    // they force through the roof, an empty lit one they open. litShutCarKeepsOut (off; the director's call, note 286): a lit
    // car with every door and its hatch shut keeps them out, and they go on over it (to the cab, with every car lit and shut
    // as the train leaves the yard).
    "mountBelow": 14, "waitForSlowSeconds": 30, "atSpeedWeight": 0.25, "tightBendRadius": 350, "bendAheadM": 300, "bendWeight": 3,
    "litShutCarKeepsOut": false
  },

  // THE GAUNT · sound (silence) · outside (App. A.6, B.6). Asleep; stirs at stirAt m, wakes at wakeAt m and follows its
  // waker at followAt m. Every silenceSeconds with nobody talking (voice above talkingAbove, 0-255) within listenRadius,
  // its anger climbs one; at attackAt it attacks. Led into a car, it takes the most valuable thing there (or, with none,
  // lootCargo of the best load) and leaves: out through the car's nearest door and off into the dark at leaveSpeed (m/s,
  // "walking pace", App. A.6), in full view: clutched under its body by the hips, hanging carryHigh m up as it stalks
  // and carryLow as it creeps aboard (the sac's underside in each, tools/blender/gaunt.py); it's gone with it once it's
  // clearedAt m from the train. Kill it before then and it drops it.
  // anyVoiceCounts: whose voice holds it off (GDD Part Eleven Q9, open): anyone's (true) or only its waker's.
  // Note 272 (App. F.1, no chip damage): its blows are heavy hits, 60 every 4 s (were 35 every 2): two, then the crush.
  "gaunt": {
    "stirAt": 9, "wakeAt": 4, "followAt": 1.2, "followSpeed": 3, "listenRadius": 8, "silenceSeconds": 5, "talkingAbove": 40,
    "anyVoiceCounts": true, "attackAt": 4, "reach": 1.6, "hitDamage": 60, "hitEvery": 4, "grabBelowHealth": 35,
    "crushSeconds": 8, "health": 8, "lootCargo": 0.3, "lingerSeconds": 900, "minCrew": 2, "spawnOut": 25,
    "longStopWeight": 2, "longStopSeconds": 120, "leaveSpeed": 1.4, "clearedAt": 30, "carryHigh": 1.7,
    "carryLow": 0.55,
    // Note 288 (drivenOff; "keep talking to it"). talkingCalms: talk brings its anger down a step every silenceSeconds (Part
